{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And now, because</b> — Some say: כי in <b>פש</b> [in the form פש] is from the root of rest [מנוחה], and it is defective of nun from וינפש. The sense is: because Job has no understanding, He visited His anger, and He did not know, for His rest is great [i.e., His reward of rest]. And some say: because you did not travail for Him, He visited His anger upon you." "<b>And did not know</b> in <b>פש</b> — They interpreted it as from the root of פרה ורבה פושו וסגו, and like it. And 'you shall go out and <b>פשתם</b>.' The sense is that He kept silent and did not visit His anger in judgment, as though He did not know due to the multitude of your words."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra appears to read כי in the word פשתם or similar in the verse; the Hebrew citation 'בפש' is opaque and may reflect a corrupt or abbreviated reference. Rendered hyper-literally.", 1 "'פרה ורבה פושו וסגו' is a rabbinic idiom (cf. Mishnah Ohalot); left untranslated as it functions here as a lexical citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:40.227409352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}